# ==========================================================
# Dashboard-local ignores — SECRETS ONLY.
#
# The repository root .gitignore is the single source of truth and already
# covers venvs, __pycache__, build output, IAM renders and OS noise. Those rules
# are NOT repeated here: two files carrying the same patterns drift, and a rule
# that quietly stopped matching is how generated IAM policies with a live
# account ID got committed once already.
#
# What remains is deliberate redundancy for the one category where a miss is
# unrecoverable, and it keeps this folder safe if it is ever extracted into a
# repository of its own.
# ==========================================================

# Real values. The .example template must still ship.
.streamlit/secrets.toml
secrets.toml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Rendered IAM policies — generated, and they embed a concrete AWS account ID.
iam/out/
